### 4.4 Quality Metrics Interpretation

| Metric | Target | Acceptable | Poor | Interpretation |
|--------|--------|------------|------|----------------|
| **F1 Score** | > 0.90 | > 0.85 | < 0.80 | Harmonic mean of precision and recall |
| **Recall** | > 0.95 | > 0.90 | < 0.85 | Attack detection rate (security critical) |
| **Precision** | > 0.85 | > 0.80 | < 0.75 | Attack prediction accuracy |
| **False Positive Rate** | < 5% | < 10% | > 15% | Normal traffic misclassified as attack |
| **False Negative Rate** | < 5% | < 10% | > 15% | Attacks misclassified as normal |
| **ROC-AUC** | > 0.95 | > 0.90 | < 0.85 | Overall discriminative power |

**If Targets Not Met**:
1. Check for data leakage (bias in features, scaler fitted on all data)
2. Increase dataset size (generate more diverse scenarios)
3. Tune hyperparameters (hidden_channels, dropout, learning_rate)
4. Verify feature extraction matches training expectations
5. Analyze failure cases (which scenarios cause errors?)

